meta {
  name: 02 Get usage
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/centers/me/usage
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.seatsUsed: eq 0
  res.body.seatsLimit: eq 1
  res.body.seatsAvailable: eq 1
  res.body.perTier[0].tier: eq START
  res.body.perTier[0].seatsHeld: eq 1
}

docs {
  A seat USED is a student row carrying this center id, counted on every read
  rather than stored — so there is no counter that can drift away from the
  students it claims to describe.

  A seat HELD is a `center_seats` row. That table is the only authority on how
  many seats a center has; `center_subscriptions.seats` used to hold a rival
  number and was removed, because two places each claiming to know the seat
  count meant nobody could say which was true.

  A fresh center holds exactly one START seat, priced at zero — its trial. So
  `seatsLimit` is 1 until it buys more.

  ## perTier is the useful half

      "perTier": [
        { "tier": "START",   "seatsHeld": 2, "seatsUsed": 2, "seatsAvailable": 0 },
        { "tier": "PRO",     "seatsHeld": 5, "seatsUsed": 1, "seatsAvailable": 4 }
      ]

  A seat belongs to a tier, so the total alone cannot answer the question a
  center actually has. "Two seats left" is useless to a school holding three
  tiers and full in one of them — and a full tier is exactly what provisioning
  refuses on. Cheapest first, always.

  A tier appears if the center holds seats in it OR has students in it. Drop a
  tier while students still sit in it:

      DELETE FROM center_seats WHERE center_id = '...' AND tier = 'PRO';

  and the PRO row stays, reporting `seatsHeld: 0` with `seatsUsed: 3`. That
  overage is what a dashboard needs to show, not hide.

  ## Buying more seats

  `center_seats` is unique per (center, tier), so buying more of a tier raises
  the quantity rather than adding a second row:

      UPDATE center_seats SET quantity = 10 WHERE center_id = '...' AND tier = 'START';

  `seatsLimit` follows immediately.

  Two more things to verify by hand:

  - Students of a DIFFERENT center must never appear in this count. Point a
    second center's students at that center and confirm this number ignores
    them.

  - `seatsAvailable` must never go negative. Give the center more students than
    `seatsLimit` and it reports 0, not a deficit. Being over the limit blocks
    future provisioning; it does not evict anyone, and existing students keep
    working.
}
